  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 236 AM MDT Sat Oct 17 2026\n\nNo big changes in the forecast for this weekend, it looks like a \nbeautiful one if you're looking for some fantastic fall weather! \nConditions will stay dry today and tomorrow with highs creeping into \nthe low 70s in parts of the eastern Magic Valley and mid 60s \neverywhere else. Sunday will be just a couple of degrees cooler and \nwinds remain fairly light each afternoon with gusts to around 15-20 \nmph. \n\nEarly next week, we will still be watching an upper level low drop \nsouth along the West Coast. There still remains the potential for it \nto draw up some Pacific moisture to our area as early as \nTuesday/Wednesday with some isolated to scattered showers (about a \n20-30 percent chance). However, it looks more likely that any \norganized push of moisture from this system will hold off until \nThursday into Friday as the low begins to move northeast from \nsouthern California into Nevada. \n\nWith these timing changes, temperatures look to stay a bit more mild \nthrough mid week now with highs staying in the 60s through Tuesday \nand Wednesday before dropping into the 50s on Thursday and 40s for \nFriday and Saturday. Of course, all of this is still about a week \nout, so keep checking back for the latest forecast updates...after \nyou enjoy this gorgeous weekend!",
